# PIR-Based Anti-Theft Alarm System

## Description
An Arduino-based motion detection alarm system that uses a PIR (Passive Infrared) 
sensor to detect movement. When motion is detected, a buzzer is triggered instantly 
as an alert, making it a simple foundation for anti-theft or intrusion detection systems.

## Components Used
- Arduino Uno R3
- PIR Motion Sensor
- Buzzer
- Breadboard
- Jumper Wires

## Circuit Connections
| Component | Arduino Pin |
|-----------|-------------|
| PIR Sensor (OUT) | Digital Pin 13 |
| Buzzer (+) | Digital Pin 8 |

## How It Works
1. The PIR sensor continuously monitors the surrounding area for motion.
2. When motion is detected, the sensor outputs a HIGH signal.
3. The Arduino reads this signal and immediately activates the buzzer (ALARM pin).
4. When no motion is detected, the buzzer remains OFF.

